<h2 id="ha-ctrl-008-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Use duplicate friendly names in different areas, translated names and long identifiers. The selected stable IDs must remain correct after sorting or filtering.
2. Exercise empty results, a registry failure, an unavailable entity and a deleted saved entity separately. No automatic replacement or silent deletion.
3. Select mixed target kinds with an exclusion and round-trip the native value without dropping fields or expanding scope.
4. Use keyboard search, selection and removal; verify focus after removing the last selected item. Check both authorised and restricted accounts without exposing hidden data.

Record the integration/frontend version, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and evidence location. Source review and documentation checks are not live-device verification. Record unresolved native limitations explicitly; do not turn this checklist into an accessibility guarantee.

